+``Cache``) are visible on the next read. Changes that bypass it -- back-office
+tools editing the database directly (BILL-2324), or another process or
+service instance with its own ``Cache`` -- can be hidden by a cached value for
+up to ``ttl_seconds``. The service does no locking, so a read whose database
+load overlaps a write can also cache the pre-write value; that too is bounded
+by the TTL.
+
